    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nRockmount is an elegant semi-detached, double-fronted period residence which spans three levels and an impressive 273 sq. m (approx. 2,938 sq. ft) of beautifully balanced living and bedroom accommodation. Set well back from the road and offering exceptional privacy, the home is approached through automated iron gates that open onto a generous front garden with parking for up to three cars.\n\nBuilt in an era celebrated for craftsmanship and architectural charm, the property exudes character throughout. The inviting entrance hall, complete with original varnished timber floors, decorative ceiling coving, ornate cornicing, and a graceful archway, sets the tone for the refined interiors beyond. At hall level, perfect symmetry defines the four reception rooms. To the left, the interconnecting drawing and dining rooms feature polished timber floors, elegant ceiling coving with centre roses, marble fireplaces, and large sash windows overlooking both the front and rear gardens.\n\nTo the right of the hallway sit a cosy sitting room with custom entertainment unit and marble fireplace, and a separate family room/home office. A guest w.c. is conveniently positioned on the return.\n\nUpstairs, there are four generous bedrooms. The principal bedroom is ensuite and enjoys sweeping views towards Dalkey and Killiney Hills. The beautifully appointed, fully tiled family bathroom offers a stunning outlook across Dublin Bay to Howth.\n\nThe garden level is home to a superb L-shaped kitchen/breakfast/living area - the true heart of the home. The Alno cream kitchen features granite countertops, a peninsula island and a full array of modern conveniences. The adjoining living space opens through French doors onto a private, sun-filled patio and, in turn, to the front garden. This level also includes a contemporary shower room and an exceptionally spacious laundry room, which enjoys direct access to the garden.\n\nThe wonderfully private rear garden is split-level in design and thoughtfully landscaped. Two paved patio areas offer ideal spaces for morning coffee or evening entertaining, with the rear patio capturing the last of the day's sunshine. The lawn is bordered by beautifully planted beds featuring Hydrangea Annabelle, mature shrubs, and trees set against a striking granite wall backdrop. A sleek, modern garden shed provides ample storage for bicycles and outdoor furniture.\n\nLocated in the heart of Dalkey, Rockmount is just a short stroll from the vibrant main street, with its charming shops, gourmet restaurants, cozy cafés, and welcoming pubs. Excellent transport links are at your doorstep, including the DART and bus services, ensuring seamless connectivity to the city and beyond.\n\nFamilies will appreciate the selection of top-tier primary and secondary schools nearby, including Harold Boys, St. Patrick's, Castle Park, Loreto Dalkey, Holy Child, and Rathdown.\n\nFor those with an active lifestyle, the surrounding area offers breathtaking coastal, and hill walks at Dalkey and Killiney Hills, invigorating sea swimming spots at Vico Road and Coliemore Harbour, and a wealth of sporting facilities, including: Cuala GAA Club, Sandycove Tennis Club and four sailing clubs in nearby Dún Laoghaire."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nvarnished original timber floors, ceiling coving and centre rose, dado rail. Front door with overhead fan light.\n\nDrawing Room - \nbeautifully appointed interconnecting reception room again with varnished original timber floors, picture rail, ceiling coving and centre rose, black marble fireplace with tiled inset and open fire.\n\nDining Room - \nanother beautifully appointed interconnecting reception room again with varnished original timber floors, picture rail, ceiling coving and centre rose, black marble fireplace with tiled inset.\n\nSitting Room - \nwonderfully comfortable sitting room with laminate wide plank oak floor, marble fireplace with open fire and picture rail. Fitted entertainment unit with shelving.\n\nFamily Room'Home Office - \ncosy double aspect room family room with laminate wide plank oak floors\n\nGuest w.c: - \nwith w.c. and wash hand basin.\n\nLower Garden Level - \n\n\nLaundry Room - \nsuperb laundry room with wide plank timber floor and eye level fitted unit and open shelving, cloaks cupboards and extensive storage. Stainless steel sink unit with single drainer. Door to rear garden.\n\nShower Room - \ncomplete with w.c., wash hand basin and shower unit\n\nKitchen/dining/living - \nAlno fitted kitchen with a selection of floor and eye level units and larder cupboards, granite countertops and peninsula island. This area has generous storage in the living room area also in both cupboard form and indeed a fully fitted entertainment unit. The kitchen is complete with Samsung American style fridge freezer, Bosch dishwasher, Britannia chrome range with six ring gas warmer and hot plate and overhead extractor fan. Siemens electric combination oven. Cream ceramic tile with overhead recessed lighting. The dining area enjoys access to the rear garden via French doors.\n\nUpstairs - \n\n\nBathroom - \nstunning part tiled family bathroom with large picture window enjoying superb sea views over to Howth. The bathroom is fully complete with bath and overhead shower, w.c. with concealed cistern, wash hand basin and vanity unit and mirrored medicine cabinet with overhead light. Three large storage cabinets and linen cupboard. Cream antique style radiator.\n\nBedroom 1 - \nnicely appointed main bedroom with fitted wardrobes, picture rail and views to Killiney & Dalkey Hills.\n\nEnsuite - \npart tiled shower unit, wash hand basin and vanity unit with medicine cabinet and overhead light and wc. Skylight.\n\nBedroom 2 - \ndirectly across from the bathroom this double room overlooks the garden and enjoys sea views to Howth.\n\nBedroom 3 - \ndouble room to the front of the house.\n\nBedroom 4 - \ngenerous single room.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Special Features</li><li> Beautifully presented double front period family home</li><li> Nicely appointed reception rooms and generous bedroom accommodation</li><li> Numerous period features such as sash windows, high ceiling heights, ceiling coving, picture rails, antique fireplaces and working shutters</li><li> Secure off street car parking to the front behind automated gates</li><li> Electric Car Charger</li><li> Spacious floor area of 273 sq. m (2,938 sq. ft approx.)</li><li> Private and tastefully landscaped rear garden with side access</li><li> Sun terraces in both front and rear gardens</li><li> Highly desirable location just a gentle stroll from Dalkey main street</li><li> Close to excellent schools, transport links and sea swimming spots</li><li> Underfloor heating throughout basement</li><li> Integrated Speaker system</ul>"
      },
